# Channel coding

This branch adds redundancy that corrects errors. `ConvolutionalCode` describes a feed-forward code, `encode` encodes with termination and `decode` decodes with soft or hard values. `gallager`, `encode` and `decode` give Gallager low-density parity-check codes with min-sum decoding, and `shuffle`, `encode` and `decode` give turbo codes with iterative max-log-MAP decoding.

## Choosing A Surface

Encode before `modulate`, decode after `llr`: the log-likelihood ratios of the demapper are the soft input of `decode`.

